[99.945367, "i", "cat FIX_SUMMARY.txt\n"]
[99.945468, "o", "cat FIX_SUMMARY.txt\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[99.946339, "o", "TIMEZONE BUG FIX SUMMARY\r\n========================\r\n\r\nPROBLEM:\r\n--------\r\nThe scheduler app was sending meeting reminders at incorrect times for meetings\r\noccurring during DST transitions (specifically 2am-3am local time in Berlin).\r\nThe Monday 2:30am maintenance window reminder was being sent at the wrong time.\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\n-----------\r\nIn app.py, the convert_to_berlin() function was incorrectly using:\r\n  berlin_dt = BERLIN_TZ.localize(utc_dt)\r\n\r\nThis treats the UTC datetime as if it's already in Berlin time and just adds"]
[99.946362, "o", "\r\nthe timezone info, rather than converting FROM UTC TO Berlin time.\r\n\r\nDuring DST transitions (like March 31, 2024 in Europe), this caused a 2-hour\r\noffset in the converted time.\r\n\r\nFIX APPLIED:\r\n------------\r\nChanged the convert_to_berlin() function to properly convert from UTC:\r\n  utc_dt = UTC_TZ.localize(utc_dt)        # Mark as UTC\r\n  berlin_dt = utc_dt.astimezone(BERLIN_TZ)  # Convert to Berlin\r\n\r\nThis ensures proper timezone conversion with correct DST handling.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLE:\r\n--------\r\nMaintenance Window Prep meeting: 2024-03-31T01:30:00 UTC\r\n- OLD (buggy): Converted to 01:30:00+01:00 Berlin (WRONG)\r\n- NEW (fixed): Converts to 03:30:00+02:00 Berlin (CORRECT)\r\n\r\nVERIFICATION:"]
[99.946463, "o", "\r\n-------------\r\nRun: python3 verification_test.py\r\nAll timezone conversions now handle DST transitions correctly.\r\n\r\nFILES MODIFIED:\r\n---------------\r\n- app.py (backup saved as app.py.backup)\r\n\r\nCRON JOB:\r\n---------\r\nAlready installed and active. Runs hourly at: 0 * * * *\r\nNo changes needed to crontab.\r\n"]
[99.946537, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[99.946579, "o", "user@27e1f8e94251:~/scheduler$ "]
